 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Order of events from the WSGI call to the view (all in `src/tessel/app.py` unless noted):\n\n1. `Tessel.__call__` → `Tessel.wsgi_entry(environ, start_response)` (~L1566).\n2. `Tessel.request_context(environ)` → `AppContext.from_environ` (`src/tessel/ctx.py`). It builds the request object and calls `build_url_binder(request)`, which creates the bound `MapAdapter`.\n3. `ctx.push()` (`src/tessel/ctx.py`):\n   - Sets `_app_var` and sends `appcontext_pushed`.\n   - Opens the session via `_get_session`.\n   - Calls `match_request()`, which sets `request.url_rule` and `request.view_args`, or `request.routing_exception`.\n4. `run_full_request(ctx)`:\n   - Sends `request_started`.\n   - `preprocess_request` runs the `url_value_preprocessor`s, then the `before_request` funcs. A non-None return from a `before_request` func short-circuits the view.\n   - `run_view` raises any stored routing exception. It handles auto-OPTIONS via `make_default_options_response`. Otherwise it calls `ensure_sync(view_functions[rule.endpoint])(**view_args)`, which is the view function.\n\nIf an exception is raised along the way, it goes to `route_user_fault`, then `route_http_fault` or a registered handler (found by `_pick_fault_handler` in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py`).",
